    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
## What it does

Evaluates one Kraken baseline and region segmentation model using `ketos segtest`.
Use held-out pages that were not used for training or model selection to estimate
segmentation quality.

## Inputs

Supply segmentation weights (Safetensors or CoreML) or a checkpoint from Ketos
Segtrain, and page images paired with PAGE XML or ALTO annotations. Automatic XML
mode accepts either format, including mixed inputs.

Select pairs individually or as a `list:paired` collection: the forward element
is the image and the reverse element is its annotation. The tool updates XML
image references for the job. Split multi-page TIFF images into single pages first.
Upload checkpoints as binary data (or ZIP) to preserve their container.

## Evaluation options

Baseline detection tolerance controls how closely predicted baselines must match
the annotations. It defaults to 10 pixels.

Full mapping uses the checkpoint's training class mappings, including merged
classes, and falls back to canonical mappings for weights. Canonical mapping
uses the model's one-to-one class mapping. Custom mapping maps annotation class
names to existing model output labels; it does not add model classes. Labels 0
and 1 are reserved. Baseline and region labels must not overlap. Reuse labels
to merge types, or use * as a fallback for unlisted types. Empty mappings disable
that category; unlisted types without a fallback are ignored.

## Output

The text report contains class mapping diagnostics, pixel accuracy and
intersection-over-union (IOU) for auxiliary and region classes, and baseline
detection precision, recall, and F1 when baseline classes are evaluated.
Inspect mapping diagnostics when annotation classes differ from model classes.

Kraken is licensed under the Apache-2.0 license.
    ]]></help>
